From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:28:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] imx6sx-blaze: set the PFUZE3000 LDOs

The product's bootloader sets three of the PFUZE3000's LDOs: V33 to
3.00 V, VCC_SD to 3.30 V, and VLDO4 to 1.80 V and off in standby. Set
them the same way.

On the MC34PF3000A3 fitted here those voltages are the OTP defaults, so
the one register change is VLDO4's standby bit. Standby is never entered
on this board, so that bit has no effect either. Setting the voltages
keeps the rails right on a board fitted with another OTP variant.

V33 supplies the SoC's VDD_HIGH_IN, VCC_SD supplies VDDA_ADC_3P3, and
VLDO4 supplies the Wi-Fi module's 1.8 V I/O.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific]
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
 board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c b/board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c
index 0a371db21a5..4877fa3d42e 100644
--- a/board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c
+++ b/board/freescale/mx6sxsabresd/mx6sxsabresd.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include <netdev.h>
 #include <power/pmic.h>
 #include <power/pfuze100_pmic.h>
+#include <power/pfuze3000_pmic.h>
 #include "../common/pfuze.h"
 #include <usb.h>
 #include <usb/ehci-ci.h>
@@ -268,6 +269,31 @@ int power_init_board(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 #elif defined(CONFIG_DM_PMIC_PFUZE100)
+#define PFUZE3000_LDO_EN	BIT(4)
+#define PFUZE3000_LDO_STBY	BIT(5)
+#define PFUZE3000_V33_3V0	0x1
+#define PFUZE3000_VCC_SD_3V3	0x3
+#define PFUZE3000_VLDO_1V8	0x0
+
+/*
+ * V33 (VDD_HIGH_IN) 3.0 V, VCC_SD (VDDA_ADC_3P3) 3.3 V, VLDO4 (Wi-Fi I/O)
+ * 1.8 V and off in standby. Other bits keep their OTP values.
+ */
+static void pfuze3000_init_ldos(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = pmic_clrsetbits(dev, PFUZE3000_V33CTL, 0x3,
+			      PFUZE3000_LDO_EN | PFUZE3000_V33_3V0);
+	ret |= pmic_clrsetbits(dev, PFUZE3000_VCC_SDCTL, 0x3,
+			       PFUZE3000_LDO_EN | PFUZE3000_VCC_SD_3V3);
+	ret |= pmic_clrsetbits(dev, PFUZE3000_VLD4CTL, 0xf,
+			       PFUZE3000_LDO_EN | PFUZE3000_LDO_STBY |
+			       PFUZE3000_VLDO_1V8);
+	if (ret)
+		printf("PMIC:  failed to set the PFUZE3000 LDOs\n");
+}
+
 int power_init_board(void)
 {
 	struct udevice *dev;
@@ -275,13 +301,14 @@ int power_init_board(void)
 	int ret;
 
 	/* PFUZE3000: its standby and mode registers decode differently from the
-	 * PFUZE100/200 sequence below, and its rails are correct from reset. */
+	 * PFUZE100/200 sequence below, so it only gets its LDOs set. */
 	ret = pmic_get("pfuze100@8", &dev);
 	if (!ret) {
 		dev_id = pmic_reg_read(dev, PFUZE100_DEVICEID);
 		if (dev_id == 0x30) {
 			printf("PMIC:  PFUZE3000 DEV_ID=0x%x REV_ID=0x%x\n",
 			       dev_id, pmic_reg_read(dev, PFUZE100_REVID));
+			pfuze3000_init_ldos(dev);
 			return 0;
 		}
 	}
-- 
